<custom_item>
  type        : AUDIT_VM
  description : "1.22 VMCH-80-000211"
  info        : "Virtual machines (VMs) must remove unneeded parallel devices.

GROUP ID: V-258724RULE ID: SV-258724r959010

Ensure no device is connected to a virtual machine if it is not required. For example, floppy, serial, and parallel ports are rarely used for virtual machines in a data center environment, and CD/DVD drives are usually connected only temporarily during software installation."
  solution    : "Parallel devices are no longer visible through the vSphere Client and must be done via the Application Programming Interface (API) or PowerCLI.

The VM must be powered off to remove a parallel device.

From a PowerCLI command prompt while connected to the ESXi host or vCenter server, run the following commands:

$pport = (Get-VM -Name ).ExtensionData.Config.Hardware.Device | Where {$_.DeviceInfo.Label -match \"Parallel\"}$spec = New-Object VMware.Vim.VirtualMachineConfigSpec$spec.DeviceChange += New-Object VMware.Vim.VirtualDeviceConfigSpec$spec.DeviceChange[-1].device = $pport$spec.DeviceChange[-1].operation = \"remove\"(Get-VM -Name ).ExtensionData.ReconfigVM($spec)"
  reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258724r959010_rule,STIG-ID|VMCH-80-000211,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258724"
  see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23620"
  xsl_stmt    : "<xsl:template match=\"//audit:returnval\">"
  xsl_stmt    : "<xsl:variable name=\"ipaddress\" select=\"audit:propSet/audit:val[@xsi:type='VirtualMachineSummary']/audit:guest/audit:ipAddress\"/>"
  xsl_stmt    : "<xsl:variable name=\"vmname\" select=\"audit:propSet/audit:val[@xsi:type='VirtualMachineConfigInfo']/audit:name\"/>"
  xsl_stmt    : "<xsl:for-each select=\"audit:propSet/audit:val[@xsi:type='VirtualMachineConfigInfo']/audit:hardware/audit:device\">"
  xsl_stmt    : "<xsl:value-of select=\"$vmname\"/> (<xsl:value-of select=\"$ipaddress\"/>) - <xsl:value-of select=\"@xsi:type\"/> : <xsl:value-of select=\"audit:deviceInfo/audit:label\"/><xsl:text>&#10;</xsl:text>"
  xsl_stmt    : "</xsl:for-each>"
  xsl_stmt    : "</xsl:template>"
  regex       : "VirtualParallelPort"
  not_expect  : "VirtualParallelPort"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : AUDIT_VM
  description : "1.23 VMCH-80-000212"
  info        : "Virtual machines (VMs) must remove unneeded serial devices.

GROUP ID: V-258725RULE ID: SV-258725r959010

Ensure no device is connected to a virtual machine if it is not required. For example, floppy, serial, and parallel ports are rarely used for virtual machines in a data center environment, and CD/DVD drives are usually connected only temporarily during software installation."
